{
	"Strada": {
		"Version": 3,
		"Type": "VisualScript"
	},
	"VisualScript": {
		"Description": "The feature test's visual script. Event.Create runs a check of every built-in node kind but the contact and click events (Contacts.sgraph and Clicks.sgraph have those), each reported through TestReporter by the function Check: Checks counts the passed ones and Done is set after the last. The waiting kinds come last, since each suspends the checks after it. The input events count into InputEvents (test runs have no input). The custom event Add adds its Amount to Score: the graph raises it with Event.Send, VisualScriptTests from C#. The custom event Retrigger enters a RetriggerableDelay, which the graph raises twice. It also checks the game's [VisualNode] members, the library MathLibrary.sgraph's functions and other graphs: it sends Ping to the falling box's Contacts.sgraph, reads and writes its Pings, and broadcasts Ping to every Contacts graph. An override of the input action Throttle presses and releases it, which Event.ActionPressed and Event.ActionReleased count and the action queries read. A Timeline plays beside the later checks, which wait for it before Done, and a curve asset and a physics material, as literals and loaded by path, after it; a raycast and sphere, box and capsule casts onto the physics material probe name the material they hit. A source it makes plays one-shots, the scene a clip at a point, and it reads the project's mixer and sets the game's values of its Voices bus. It marks its start and its first step for telemetry and records its fixed steps as Features.FixedSteps. It saves a slot of its own, held in a variable, reads it back through another and deletes it, and sets, reads and removes a value of the player's settings. It rides the scene's Bike from its fixed steps (VehicleComponent: the throttle in the first gear, then both brakes), resets it once it stands, and sets BikeRidden when the ride has ended, for VehicleTests to ride it next.",
